{"skill":{"slug":"deepread-ocr","displayName":"DeepRead OCR"},"version":{"version":"1.1.0","createdAt":1774973791607,"changelog":"Added BYOK section and cross-links to all DeepRead skills (form-fill, PII, agent-setup, BYOK).","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":18160,"sha256":"47495c7ec643997dc0cc3e1d504a5048cbb93798c2edf89010803bd6888b3f44","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"_meta.json","size":131,"sha256":"4110a85d3bdecc80c86334159f67676590061f3499cab89b3f4ad69bcf8711b8","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"package.json","size":619,"sha256":"556aa06c3ba7c98b7d6ca711a0bc6f4e472ac2cc55598fdd57ab503daf292053","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2313,"sha256":"d39fa618c73ea54a968f9e6737154ea794cd1116919041cbe5d47f0256f8fef3","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789024308562,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"d7cec7c3fa1f7c61c95b6fa903d5608efb6670d78ccace7325aefd5206614c6e","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/d7cec7c3fa1f7c61c95b6fa903d5608efb6670d78ccace7325aefd5206614c6e","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: deepread-ocr\nVersion: 1.1.0\n\nThe skill is a legitimate integration for the DeepRead OCR service, providing instructions and examples for document processing and structured data extraction via the api.deepread.tech endpoints. It follows standard practices for API-based skills, requiring an environment variable for authentication and containing no evidence of malicious execution, data exfiltration, or prompt injection.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160395822},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":65,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":25,"checkedAt":1789024308562},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This OCR skill is mostly coherent, but its unauthenticated public preview links can expose uploaded document contents to anyone who has the URL.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Requiring an API key and sending selected documents to an OCR SaaS endpoint is proportionate for this skill, but users need to treat uploaded files, schemas, webhook payloads, BYOK provider routing, and preview URLs as sensitive data flows.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The package contains only SKILL.md, package.json, and _meta.json, with no executable files, install scripts, dependency tree, or local code payload.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The instructions are documentation-only and do not contain prompt hijacking or hidden agent commands, but they repeatedly encourage uploading invoices, contracts, and training documents without a prominent privacy warning at first use.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No artifact evidence shows local persistence, privilege escalation, background workers, scheduled tasks, memory writes, credential scraping, or destructive local actions.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill's core purpose is document OCR through DeepRead's external API, which matches the documented curl examples and required DEEPREAD_API_KEY. The concern is the preview feature: it can include original document images and is documented as shareable without authentication.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Review DeepRead's privacy, retention, BYOK, and preview-link controls before installing. Do not use public previews or webhooks for sensitive documents unless your organization accepts that anyone with a preview URL may be able to view the document preview, and only upload regulated, confidential, or customer documents under an approved data-processing arrangement.","findings":"[SQP-2] unexpected: Verified for the public preview section: the artifact states preview URLs can be shared without authentication and shows a no-auth preview endpoint, which is under-scoped for sensitive OCR documents.\n[SQP-2] expected: Verified for first-use upload examples: external document processing is expected for an OCR API skill, but the documentation should more clearly disclose third-party handling of document contents and extracted results.\n[E1] expected: The repeated api.deepread.tech uploads are purpose-aligned external API use, not hidden exfiltration; the residual concern is user awareness around sensitive documents, schemas, training data, webhooks, and BYOK providers.\n[E1] unexpected: The preview endpoint example materially expands exposure because document previews are accessible without an API key once the URL is known.\n[EA2] expected: The auto-approval language refers to high-confidence OCR fields being marked as not requiring human review, not autonomous destructive actions or financial transactions; this is expected for the stated HIL workflow.\n[SDI-2] unexpected: Verified: unauthenticated preview sharing is explicitly documented and creates a real confidentiality concern for invoices, contracts, forms, and other sensitive documents.\n[T09] unexpected: The static scan's public-preview concern is supported by the artifact: the documented preview URL works as a bearer link with no separate authentication.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789024308562}}}}}